  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Read the main path",
      "items": [
        "Discord sends a command → Traefik routes it to the bot → the bot reads or changes guild data.",
        "The browser uses the same HTTPS entry to show the dashboard after signing in with Discord.",
        "The bot also receives Discord events and collects public Foxhole state for the war log."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What supports operations",
      "items": [
        "PostgreSQL holds shared state. Each guild’s data stays isolated; replicas coordinate their work in the database.",
        "The voice journal recovers events after a crash. Bot and dashboard share it to apply erasure.",
        "Backups are encrypted: at most five archives, none older than 30 days. Voice history is excluded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Options and stack details",
      "items": [
        "The dashboard is enabled with DASHBOARD_HOST. Monitoring is enabled with the monitoring profile.",
        "Monitoring: Grafana displays Prometheus metrics and Loki logs; Alloy and three exporters collect them.",
        "Traefik also serves Grafana. Certificates use Cloudflare DNS-01; secrets stay in dedicated files.",
        "Migration, deployment, purge and restore are operational tools. Their details are below the diagram.",
        "Boxes group responsibilities. The full list of containers, ports, networks and volumes is on the page."
      ]
    }
  ]
